 <b2210356065@cs.hacettepe.edu.tr>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 16:33:07 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 46/71] Remove the pre-compaction AGENTS.md memory refresh

The refresh was one ordinary agent turn, run invisibly before every
compaction. On the measured sessions it made 3-10 requests at the very top
of the window, each resending 80-100K tokens, which put it at roughly ten
times the cost of the one-request summarization it preceded. The rounds went
to reading linked files that did not exist, a patch shape apply_patch
rejects, verification reads, and in one case re-running code to check a
finding.

Upstream keeps AGENTS.md read-only and carries durable memory through its
detached memories pipeline instead, which runs outside the live context.
This fork now does the same. The invisible-turn plumbing stays, since
app-server turns still use it; only the parent-context fork that this turn
alone needed goes with it, along with the `project_memory` feature flag and
the prompt template.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
